Ask the local LLAMA model for a read-only second opinion, preliminary research, brainstorming, or loss-aware compression. Compression uses internal map-reduce rather than truncating the source.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__llama_advisor__ask_llama(args: {
  // Optional supporting context.
  context?: string;
  // How LLAMA should approach the request.
  purpose?: "compress" | "review" | "research" | "brainstorm";
  // The specific question or task for LLAMA.
  task: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Use compression as read-only, loss-aware orientation. A single compression tool call may internally map and reduce multiple chunks. Trust coverage_complete only when input_truncated and output_truncated are both false. Verify cited original lines for security, permissions, destructive actions, numerical conclusions, and code changes.

Read project text files and produce a complete, cited digest. Long inputs are split by file and line, summarized, and hierarchically reduced. The call fails instead of returning a silently truncated digest when coverage cannot be proven.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__llama_advisor__compress_files(args: {
  // Optional topic the digest should emphasize without dropping coverage.
  focus?: string;
  // Digest language: source language, Japanese, or English.
  output_language?: "source" | "ja" | "en";
  // Project-relative text file paths to compress.
  paths: Array<string>;
  // Absolute project root. Files outside its canonical path are rejected.
  project_root: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```
